From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:54:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: aoc: port Google's AoC core to gs201 on Linux
 7.3

Build Google's AoC core, mailbox and service character devices on this
kernel and wire them to the gs201 pieces already here:

 - firmware: GSA load (mailbox) and start through Trusty's hwmgr.aoc
   (gsa.c), the AoC S2MPU opened and the System MMU windows from the
   image header installed (gs201-aoc-sysmmu) once aoc_req is
   acknowledged;
 - vendor interfaces without a mainline counterpart (debug-snapshot,
   power modes, PMU, ACPM channel 13, sscoredump, ITMON, physical
   dma-buf heaps) stubbed in aoc-compat.h; crash restart off by default
   (aoc_disable_restart), no panic on aoc_req time-outs;
 - the AoC SRAM is not mapped (its registers abort with the A32 in
   reset); gs201 constants replace the vendor DT properties; chip ids
   read from the chip id block;
 - 7.3 API updates (bus match, class_create, devnode, void remove,
   sched_set_fifo_low).

Bindings: the AoC mailbox blocks (google,gs201-aoc-mbox) and the AoC
node's 48 mailbox channels, through which the bring-up driver finds the
mailboxes. The device tree nodes come with the AoC's own commit.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
